+      "current cell and a closed identity are different statements (that is the whole defect)",
+      _r4["history_unresolved"] is True and _r4["distance"] == 1.0
+      and RC.feasible_exact(_b1, T, [0.0, 0.0, 1.0])["history_unresolved"] is False,
+      {"1->0": _r4["history_unresolved"],
+       "0->1": RC.feasible_exact(_b1, T, [0.0, 0.0, 1.0])["history_unresolved"]})
+
+print("\n[G4] the Q6 shape itself — the defect that opened the item")
+# PREREG §0 / §3.1: two requests EXPIRED at 25 each (so 50 is explained), read back 80, next anchor
+# no fills, read back 80. The live reconciler calls window 2 CLEAN. Here the 30 must not vanish.
+# ★ BIRTH AFTER t_0, TERMINAL BEFORE t_1. The two top-ups did not exist at the baseline readback
+#   (so x_i(t_0) = 0 by constraint (a), which is what makes the baseline a baseline) and were
+#   already closed when the 80 was read. Giving them birth=t_0 would leave x_i(t_0) free, and the
+#   identity is stated as a CHANGE since t_0 — a free baseline lets the whole 80 be explained as
+#   "already there", which is the very absorption this item exists to stop.
