+# BEFORE the terminal evidence lands, a BUY100 with 100 of capacity explains 80 outright.
+_no_ev = RC.feasible_exact([RC.Request("u", +1, 100.0, birth=0.25)], T, [0.0, 80.0, 80.0], step=10.0)
+# AFTER it lands (credible total 50), the same readings leave 30 unexplained — and because the
+# distance is recomputed from the CUMULATIVE identity over the whole prefix, it does not matter at
+# which anchor we were told: the answer is a function of the evidence set, not of arrival order.
+_ev = RC.feasible_exact([RC.Request("u", +1, 100.0, birth=0.25, terminal=0.5, exact=50.0)],
+                        T, [0.0, 80.0, 80.0], step=10.0)
+check("★★★ G4b late evidence NARROWS the same request rather than creating a second execution: with "
+      "no terminal total, 100 of capacity explains 80 (distance 0, history clean); with a credible "
+      "total of 50, the same two readings leave 30 — computed from the cumulative identity over the "
+      "whole prefix, so it is a function of the EVIDENCE SET and not of which window the evidence "
+      "arrived in (the literal per-window recursion the PREREG rejects gives -50 in one order and "
+      "+30 in the other for the same final facts)",
+      _no_ev["distance"] == 0.0 and not _no_ev["history_unresolved"]
+      and _ev["distance"] == 30.0 and _ev["predicted"] == [50.0],
+      {"before": (_no_ev["distance"], _no_ev["history_unresolved"]),
+       "after": (_ev["distance"], _ev["predicted"])})
+
