+#   one slips through — lo = hi = exact is not "lo > hi", so the domain would simply be a value the
+#   request could never reach. (Found by a mutant that removed the check and left the suite green;
+#   the exact-below-floor case above is caught by monotonicity even without it, this one is not.)
+_over = [RC.Request("x", +1, 1.0, birth=0.25, terminal=0.5, exact=2.0)]
+_ro = RC.feasible_exact(_over, T, [0.0, 2.0, 2.0])
